{
  "v": 3,
  "about": "K133 + G3-1: the one definition of 'Apple container is installed', read by the app (electron/iclone-confinement/probe.test.ts) and the Hermes plugin (tests/plugins/test_iclone_confinement.py), each held to the same verdict per case. Installed = Apple silicon on macOS 26 or later (Darwin 25+) AND the first fixed path that exists (in this order; PATH never counts) AND that file is executable AND `--version` exits 0 within the timeout with stdout in the CLI's own format (versionPattern, anchored at the start: not any x.y.z anywhere). A --version that does not finish in time is `unknown` / `probe-timeout` (neutral: could not check, G3-2), never broken; red is for a definite failure only. `seen` is the clause both sides put in the spawn refusal. G3 r2 m-1: every answer is RAW BYTES (`stdoutBytes`/`stderrBytes`: one character per byte, U+0000-U+00FF, i.e. latin-1), read by both sides with one rule (`output`): at most maxBytes per stream (more is stopped: a definite failure, `output-too-large`), decoded as UTF-8 with invalid bytes replaced, stripped of exactly \" \\t\\r\\n\", matched with ASCII digits only. `read` is the text both sides must read from those bytes (decoded and stripped), checked through the stub runner. `programs` are real files (with `stdoutLength`, the exact byte count the program prints, so the bound is pinned to the byte) each side writes and runs through its REAL runner.",
